-- title:
--   A rational canonical noncusp remains noncuspidal on the modular curve
-- statement:
--   Let $(x:y:z:w)∈ℙ^3(ℚ)$ be a nonzero solution of the canonical quadric and cubic that is not a canonical cusp. Transport its associated canonical place to $ℚ(X_H(25))$. Then $$¬Cusp_j(P_{x,y,z,w}^{X_H}).$$ This matches canonical noncusps with modular noncusps.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

